  "changes": [
    "Host-wide 96-unit burst and 8-unit/second refill caps aggregate receive and inference work across all owners",
    "Every partial-body reservation consumes a nonce and one owner/global unit; timeout and disconnect cannot replay it",
    "Complete available bodies bypass the partial-body quota and are hash-checked before consuming a ticket",
    "Owner reservations transfer from the receive queue through the worker and release on all terminal exits",
    "Both budgets receive elapsed refill at charge time and symmetric inference-failure refunds",
    "Fifteen-second request lifetime accommodates measured two-core model execution; eight-unit/second refill bounds sustained load",
    "JSON bodies decode strictly as UTF-8",
    "Deadline timer shuts down sockets; handlers own descriptor closure",
    "Budget responses advertise refill delay; the client retries only the throttled batch with a fresh ticket within a 60-second bound",
    "Preserve prior padded-tensor, canonical-protocol, immutable-dependency and CPU-provider corrections"
  ],
